## What I Learned
How to read and analyze Python source code to understand 
what a program does before running it. The flag was 
hidden using XOR encryption with a hardcoded key — 
a common obfuscation technique in CTFs and malware. 
Reading source code carefully to find dormant functions 
that are never called is a fundamental reverse 
engineering and code analysis skill used in real 
security work when analyzing suspicious scripts 
or applications.
